            <ArticleTitle>Left ventricular cannula obstruction in a patient with previous ventricular aneurysmectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1182-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cannula position is an important factor influencing optimal ventricular assist device function. A case of inflow cannula malposition resulting in suboptimal left ventricular assist device performance is presented. A discussion of alternative techniques and diagnosis is provided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
